module Main
import Base
import Borrow
-- Containment (spec 2026-08-10), R2 realized: the RECORD form of the same
-- hole. Found during implementation -- the declaration-site closure alone did
-- NOT close this, because a record's type is `CTRecord tag row` (the tag is the
-- CONSTRUCTOR name, field types live structurally in the row), so there is no
-- tycon name for the carrier predicates to look up. `data R = R Borrow` was
-- correctly rejected while `data R = R { b : Borrow }` was accepted.
--
-- Consequence if left open: a second-class foreign borrow escapes its lending
-- activation, which the Slice-3 borrow-noescape negative control demonstrates
-- is a genuine use-after-free (the activation-scoped close frees the buffer the
-- escapee then reads). Closed by answering record containment STRUCTURALLY in
-- `isHandleType`/`isAffineCarrierType` (see `recordRowCarries`).
--
-- `Borrow` is the carrier used here deliberately: it takes no type parameters,
-- and parameterized records are broken by a separate pre-existing bug
-- (`freeze: unexpected Rigid`), so a `Suspension` field cannot yet be spelled
-- in a record at all. When that bug is fixed, the affine carriers reach this
-- same route -- and this fixture is what proves the route is already shut.
data R = R { b : Borrow }
leak : R -> [R]
leak r = [r]
main : U64
main = 0
